{"seq":9,"slug":"political-violence-conflict","title":"政治暴力与冲突","stage":"DONE","category":"political-science","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 政治暴力与冲突\n\n2025 年是冷战结束以来最血腥的年份之一。乌普萨拉冲突数据项目（UCDP）记录全球有约 65 场活跃冲突、约 24.46 万人死于有组织暴力，仅次于 1994 年卢旺达种族灭绝那一年；其中国家间直接冲突翻倍至 8 场，创下 1946 年有数据以来的最高纪录。这组数字提醒我们：政治暴力不是历史的残余，而是当下世界政治的核心现象。本 hub 要回答的根本问题只有一个——为什么人群会诉诸暴力来争夺、维持或颠覆政治权力，以及这种暴力如何被点燃、维持、最终被终结。\n\n整个 hub 由四个章节构成一条由因到果、由爆发到善后的递进链条。第一章「概念与理论」是全部讨论的解释地基：它先把\"政治暴力\"这个看似不言自明的词拆开，区分直接暴力、结构性暴力与文化暴力，建立可测量的定义与数据基础设施（UCDP、ACLED、GTI），再深入两类最重要的宏观暴力——内战与武装冲突的\"贪婪对怨恨\"之争，以及革命与国家崩溃的结构性解释。后面三章遇到的任何概念，其理论根都扎在这一章。\n\n第二章「形式」把镜头对准政治暴力的主要类型：恐怖主义作为弱者的\"传播性暴力\"战略，族群冲突与种族灭绝中的安全困境与分阶段升级，以及由国家自上而下施加的镇压与国家恐怖。这三种形式共享第一章的解释逻辑，但各有独特的行为者结构与升级动力学。\n\n第三章「动员与过程」追问一个更微观的问题：暴力如何被组织起来、又靠什么维持？它从抗争政治与社会运动的宏观动员机制，下沉到个体为何参与暴力的微观基础，再落到把战争维持下去的经济与资源命脉。这一章是连接\"结构原因\"与\"实际暴力\"之间的传送带。\n\n第四章「解决与前沿」转向善后与未来：冲突如何通过谈判、调解与维和被终结，社会如何通过转型正义与重建从暴力中愈合，以及无人机、网络与人工智能正在如何重写 2025–2026 年的战争形态。读完四章，你会得到一张从\"为何爆发\"到\"如何收场\"的完整认知地图。\n\n建议顺序阅读，但每篇 L4 也可独立查阅；篇与篇之间用交叉链接织成网，便于你在\"概念—形式—过程—解决\"之间往返穿梭。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"concepts-theory","title":"概念与理论","docCount":3,"url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/concepts-theory","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-core-concepts","title":"政治暴力导论","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/concepts-theory/intro-and-core-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"civil-war-armed-conflict","title":"内战与武装冲突理论","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/concepts-theory/civil-war-armed-conflict"},{"seq":3,"slug":"revolution-state-breakdown","title":"革命与国家崩溃","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/concepts-theory/revolution-state-breakdown"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"forms","title":"形式","docCount":3,"url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/forms","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"terrorism","title":"恐怖主义","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/forms/terrorism"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ethnic-conflict-genocide","title":"族群冲突与种族灭绝","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/forms/ethnic-conflict-genocide"},{"seq":3,"slug":"state-violence-repression","title":"国家暴力与镇压","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/forms/state-violence-repression"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"mobilization-process","title":"动员与过程","docCount":3,"url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/mobilization-process","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"contentious-politics-movements","title":"抗争政治与社会运动","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/mobilization-process/contentious-politics-movements"},{"seq":2,"slug":"micro-foundations-of-violence","title":"冲突的微观基础","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/mobilization-process/micro-foundations-of-violence"},{"seq":3,"slug":"war-economies-resources","title":"冲突的经济与资源","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/mobilization-process/war-economies-resources"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"resolution-frontiers","title":"解决与前沿","docCount":3,"url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/resolution-frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"conflict-resolution-peacebuilding","title":"冲突解决与和平建设","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/resolution-frontiers/conflict-resolution-peacebuilding"},{"seq":2,"slug":"transitional-justice-reconstruction","title":"转型正义与冲突后重建","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/resolution-frontiers/transitional-justice-reconstruction"},{"seq":3,"slug":"new-wars-cyber-ai-frontiers","title":"新战争、网络与AI前沿","url":"/h/political-science/political-violence-conflict/resolution-frontiers/new-wars-cyber-ai-frontiers"}]}]}